{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":3,"title":"Path of Selfless service, Karma-yoga","narrator":{"name":"Sonia","voice":"en-GB-SoniaNeural"},"duration":529.176,"scenes":[{"layout":"title","headline":"The Path of Selfless Service","visual":["Karma-yoga: work as an offering"],"L":[],"say":"Chapter Three. The Path of Selfless Service, Karma-yoga. Krishna has praised knowledge and a calm mind. Now Arjuna asks the obvious question.","start":0.0,"at":0.576,"end":12.024,"words":[[0.1,0.5,"Chapter"],[0.613,0.525,"Three"],[1.538,0.113,"The"],[1.663,0.338,"Path"],[2.013,0.113,"of"],[2.138,0.525,"Selfless"],[2.675,0.55,"Service"],[3.462,0.825,"Karma-yoga"],[4.65,0.512,"Krishna"],[5.175,0.212,"has"],[5.4,0.438,"praised"],[5.85,0.487,"knowledge"],[6.35,0.15,"and"],[6.513,0.05,"a"],[6.575,0.312,"calm"],[6.9,0.487,"mind"],[7.763,0.287,"Now"],[8.062,0.6,"Arjuna"],[8.675,0.375,"asks"],[9.062,0.125,"the"],[9.2,0.388,"obvious"],[9.6,0.613,"question"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Then why must I fight?","visual":["If knowledge is better than action…","…why push me into this terrible deed?","Your words confuse me. Tell me one thing"],"L":[],"say":"If you think knowledge is better than action, Arjuna says, then why do you urge me into this terrible war? Your words seem mixed, and they confuse my mind. Tell me, decisively, the one thing by which I may reach the highest good. It is a fair question, and the whole chapter answers it.","start":12.024,"at":12.6,"end":31.824,"words":[[0.138,0.138,"If"],[0.287,0.113,"you"],[0.412,0.287,"think"],[0.713,0.4,"knowledge"],[1.125,0.125,"is"],[1.262,0.275,"better"],[1.55,0.138,"than"],[1.7,0.512,"action"],[2.475,0.425,"Arjuna"],[2.913,0.412,"says"],[3.625,0.188,"then"],[3.825,0.188,"why"],[4.025,0.113,"do"],[4.15,0.175,"you"],[4.338,0.275,"urge"],[4.625,0.138,"me"],[4.775,0.25,"into"],[5.037,0.175,"this"],[5.225,0.487,"terrible"],[5.725,0.388,"war"],[6.513,0.15,"Your"],[6.675,0.438,"words"],[7.125,0.237,"seem"],[7.375,0.475,"mixed"],[8.075,0.087,"and"],[8.175,0.113,"they"],[8.3,0.525,"confuse"],[8.838,0.138,"my"],[8.988,0.562,"mind"],[9.912,0.3,"Tell"],[10.225,0.25,"me"],[10.662,0.8,"decisively"],[11.725,0.075,"the"],[11.812,0.275,"one"],[12.1,0.3,"thing"],[12.412,0.15,"by"],[12.575,0.25,"which"],[12.838,0.075,"I"],[12.925,0.2,"may"],[13.137,0.325,"reach"],[13.475,0.075,"the"],[13.562,0.463,"highest"],[14.037,0.362,"good"],[14.775,0.138,"It"],[14.925,0.125,"is"],[15.062,0.075,"a"],[15.15,0.25,"fair"],[15.412,0.625,"question"],[16.288,0.1,"and"],[16.4,0.075,"the"],[16.488,0.263,"whole"],[16.762,0.438,"chapter"],[17.212,0.412,"answers"],[17.637,0.35,"it"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L13"],"ref":"3.03","verse":"The Supreme Lord said: In this world, O Arjuna, a twofold path of spiritual discipline has been stated by Me in the past — the path of Self-knowledge for the contemplative, introverts and the path of unselfish work (Seva, Karma-yoga) for all others.","key":true,"vs":[12,55],"say":"Krishna begins by saying there are two paths, not one. Verse three. The Supreme Lord said: In this world, O Arjuna, a twofold path of spiritual discipline has been stated by Me in the past — the path of Self-knowledge for the contemplative, introverts and the path of unselfish work (Seva, Karma-yoga) for all others.","start":31.824,"at":32.4,"end":54.024,"words":[[0.1,0.438,"Krishna"],[0.55,0.475,"begins"],[1.038,0.163,"by"],[1.212,0.362,"saying"],[1.587,0.087,"there"],[1.688,0.1,"are"],[1.8,0.275,"two"],[2.087,0.55,"paths"],[2.913,0.263,"not"],[3.188,0.362,"one"],[3.925,0.425,"Verse"],[4.362,0.463,"three"],[5.188,0.175,"The"],[5.375,0.45,"Supreme"],[5.838,0.237,"Lord"],[6.088,0.312,"said"],[6.638,0.113,"In"],[6.763,0.212,"this"],[6.987,0.362,"world"],[7.537,0.113,"O"],[7.662,0.588,"Arjuna"],[8.463,0.037,"a"],[8.512,0.487,"twofold"],[9.012,0.312,"path"],[9.338,0.075,"of"],[9.425,0.5,"spiritual"],[9.938,0.487,"discipline"],[10.438,0.163,"has"],[10.613,0.15,"been"],[10.775,0.412,"stated"],[11.2,0.163,"by"],[11.375,0.138,"Me"],[11.525,0.087,"in"],[11.625,0.075,"the"],[11.713,0.5,"past"],[12.325,0.1,"the"],[12.438,0.287,"path"],[12.738,0.087,"of"],[12.838,0.688,"Self-knowledge"],[13.537,0.087,"for"],[13.637,0.087,"the"],[13.738,0.8,"contemplative"],[14.825,0.6,"introverts"],[15.438,0.113,"and"],[15.562,0.087,"the"],[15.662,0.312,"path"],[15.988,0.1,"of"],[16.1,0.575,"unselfish"],[16.688,0.35,"work"],[17.288,0.487,"Seva"],[18.012,0.738,"Karma-yoga"],[18.95,0.138,"for"],[19.1,0.225,"all"],[19.337,0.463,"others"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"No one can stop acting","visual":["Not starting work does not free you","Even keeping the body alive is action","Restraining the body while the mind roams is hypocrisy"],"L":["L1","L14"],"say":"But no one, Krishna says, can live without acting, even for a moment. Nature drives every creature to act. Simply refusing to work does not set anyone free, and even keeping the body alive requires action. Worse is the person who holds the body still while the mind dwells on pleasures. Krishna calls that person a hypocrite.","start":54.024,"at":54.6,"end":77.448,"words":[[0.1,0.237,"But"],[0.35,0.212,"no"],[0.575,0.35,"one"],[1.087,0.388,"Krishna"],[1.488,0.425,"says"],[2.188,0.175,"can"],[2.375,0.2,"live"],[2.587,0.375,"without"],[2.975,0.487,"acting"],[3.688,0.263,"even"],[3.962,0.138,"for"],[4.112,0.05,"a"],[4.175,0.613,"moment"],[5.162,0.525,"Nature"],[5.7,0.525,"drives"],[6.237,0.275,"every"],[6.525,0.438,"creature"],[6.975,0.15,"to"],[7.138,0.5,"act"],[8.025,0.463,"Simply"],[8.5,0.575,"refusing"],[9.088,0.113,"to"],[9.213,0.388,"work"],[9.613,0.163,"does"],[9.787,0.212,"not"],[10.012,0.25,"set"],[10.275,0.35,"anyone"],[10.637,0.412,"free"],[11.35,0.138,"and"],[11.5,0.263,"even"],[11.775,0.35,"keeping"],[12.137,0.1,"the"],[12.25,0.35,"body"],[12.613,0.425,"alive"],[13.05,0.487,"requires"],[13.55,0.525,"action"],[14.475,0.375,"Worse"],[14.863,0.1,"is"],[14.975,0.1,"the"],[15.088,0.45,"person"],[15.55,0.138,"who"],[15.7,0.312,"holds"],[16.025,0.1,"the"],[16.137,0.4,"body"],[16.55,0.388,"still"],[16.95,0.163,"while"],[17.125,0.087,"the"],[17.225,0.4,"mind"],[17.637,0.412,"dwells"],[18.062,0.125,"on"],[18.2,0.65,"pleasures"],[19.212,0.537,"Krishna"],[19.762,0.375,"calls"],[20.15,0.237,"that"],[20.4,0.388,"person"],[20.8,0.037,"a"],[20.85,0.762,"hypocrite"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L4"],"ref":"3.09","verse":"Human beings are bound by work that is not performed as a selfless service. Therefore, O Arjuna, becoming free from attachment to the fruits of work, do your duty efficiently as a service to Me.","key":true,"vs":[16,51],"say":"So the answer is not to stop working, but to change why we work. Verse nine. Human beings are bound by work that is not performed as a selfless service. Therefore, O Arjuna, becoming free from attachment to the fruits of work, do your duty efficiently as a service to Me.","start":77.448,"at":78.024,"end":97.488,"words":[[0.125,0.2,"So"],[0.338,0.138,"the"],[0.487,0.388,"answer"],[0.887,0.125,"is"],[1.025,0.212,"not"],[1.25,0.075,"to"],[1.337,0.3,"stop"],[1.65,0.525,"working"],[2.438,0.175,"but"],[2.625,0.1,"to"],[2.737,0.412,"change"],[3.163,0.188,"why"],[3.362,0.125,"we"],[3.5,0.537,"work"],[4.4,0.438,"Verse"],[4.85,0.475,"nine"],[5.7,0.375,"Human"],[6.088,0.45,"beings"],[6.55,0.087,"are"],[6.65,0.438,"bound"],[7.1,0.163,"by"],[7.275,0.45,"work"],[7.737,0.15,"that"],[7.9,0.113,"is"],[8.025,0.225,"not"],[8.262,0.55,"performed"],[8.825,0.15,"as"],[8.988,0.062,"a"],[9.062,0.5,"selfless"],[9.575,0.625,"service"],[10.6,0.613,"Therefore"],[11.387,0.15,"O"],[11.55,0.6,"Arjuna"],[12.375,0.412,"becoming"],[12.8,0.3,"free"],[13.113,0.163,"from"],[13.287,0.65,"attachment"],[13.95,0.075,"to"],[14.037,0.087,"the"],[14.137,0.312,"fruits"],[14.463,0.1,"of"],[14.575,0.412,"work"],[15.287,0.087,"do"],[15.387,0.15,"your"],[15.55,0.438,"duty"],[16.0,0.637,"efficiently"],[16.65,0.113,"as"],[16.775,0.062,"a"],[16.85,0.412,"service"],[17.275,0.125,"to"],[17.413,0.25,"Me"]]},{"layou