"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Leaders and Wise Persons Must Set the Example","visual":["Whatever the great do, others follow","Leaders set the standard","Even God acts to set an example"],"L":["L5"],"say":"Lesson five. Leaders and wise people must set the example. Whatever noble people do, others copy, and whatever standard they set, the world follows. Krishna himself keeps acting, though he has nothing to gain, simply to keep the world on its path.","start":295.416,"at":295.992,"end":313.992,"words":[[0.113,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.575,"five"],[1.55,0.562,"Leaders"],[2.125,0.163,"and"],[2.3,0.4,"wise"],[2.712,0.438,"people"],[3.163,0.325,"must"],[3.5,0.275,"set"],[3.788,0.113,"the"],[3.913,0.688,"example"],[5.0,0.463,"Whatever"],[5.475,0.375,"noble"],[5.862,0.35,"people"],[6.225,0.375,"do"],[6.787,0.312,"others"],[7.112,0.463,"copy"],[7.85,0.113,"and"],[7.975,0.412,"whatever"],[8.4,0.438,"standard"],[8.85,0.138,"they"],[9.0,0.412,"set"],[9.613,0.087,"the"],[9.713,0.312,"world"],[10.037,0.613,"follows"],[11.012,0.438,"Krishna"],[11.463,0.55,"himself"],[12.025,0.312,"keeps"],[12.35,0.5,"acting"],[13.125,0.15,"though"],[13.287,0.125,"he"],[13.425,0.15,"has"],[13.588,0.325,"nothing"],[13.925,0.113,"to"],[14.05,0.388,"gain"],[14.725,0.412,"simply"],[15.15,0.1,"to"],[15.262,0.237,"keep"],[15.512,0.087,"the"],[15.613,0.35,"world"],[15.975,0.113,"on"],[16.1,0.15,"its"],[16.262,0.512,"path"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Nature Does All the Work — The Ego Falsely Claims It","visual":["The three gunas of nature do all the work","The ego claims to be the doer","Wrongly claimed doership creates karma"],"L":["L6"],"say":"Lesson six. Nature does all the work; the ego falsely claims it. Every action is carried out by the three forces of nature. The ego, the sense of being a separate doer, takes the credit and the blame, and that false claim is what binds us.","start":313.992,"at":314.568,"end":331.68,"words":[[0.113,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.588,"six"],[1.562,0.475,"Nature"],[2.05,0.188,"does"],[2.25,0.138,"all"],[2.4,0.087,"the"],[2.5,0.45,"work"],[3.25,0.1,"the"],[3.362,0.425,"ego"],[3.8,0.487,"falsely"],[4.3,0.4,"claims"],[4.713,0.35,"it"],[5.438,0.325,"Every"],[5.775,0.487,"action"],[6.275,0.15,"is"],[6.438,0.35,"carried"],[6.8,0.35,"out"],[7.162,0.15,"by"],[7.325,0.113,"the"],[7.45,0.287,"three"],[7.75,0.45,"forces"],[8.213,0.113,"of"],[8.338,0.55,"nature"],[9.275,0.125,"The"],[9.412,0.525,"ego"],[10.125,0.1,"the"],[10.238,0.325,"sense"],[10.575,0.113,"of"],[10.7,0.25,"being"],[10.963,0.05,"a"],[11.025,0.438,"separate"],[11.475,0.338,"doer"],[12.1,0.3,"takes"],[12.412,0.087,"the"],[12.512,0.412,"credit"],[12.938,0.087,"and"],[13.037,0.087,"the"],[13.137,0.4,"blame"],[13.85,0.075,"and"],[13.938,0.212,"that"],[14.162,0.3,"false"],[14.475,0.35,"claim"],[14.838,0.1,"is"],[14.95,0.2,"what"],[15.162,0.338,"binds"],[15.512,0.375,"us"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Do Not Unsettle the Minds of the Spiritually Immature","visual":["Don't shake the faith of those still learning","Inspire by doing your own work well","Example teaches more than argument"],"L":["L7"],"say":"Lesson seven. Do not unsettle the minds of the spiritually immature. People who are still attached to the fruits of their work should not be confused or mocked by the wise. Inspire them instead, by doing your own work well and without attachment. Example teaches more than argument.","start":331.68,"at":332.256,"end":351.6,"words":[[0.125,0.487,"Lesson"],[0.625,0.55,"seven"],[1.538,0.2,"Do"],[1.75,0.25,"not"],[2.013,0.575,"unsettle"],[2.6,0.1,"the"],[2.712,0.475,"minds"],[3.2,0.1,"of"],[3.312,0.1,"the"],[3.425,0.688,"spiritually"],[4.125,0.675,"immature"],[5.162,0.425,"People"],[5.6,0.125,"who"],[5.737,0.087,"are"],[5.838,0.312,"still"],[6.162,0.537,"attached"],[6.713,0.075,"to"],[6.8,0.1,"the"],[6.912,0.338,"fruits"],[7.263,0.1,"of"],[7.375,0.138,"their"],[7.525,0.438,"work"],[7.975,0.212,"should"],[8.2,0.225,"not"],[8.438,0.113,"be"],[8.562,0.675,"confused"],[9.25,0.125,"or"],[9.387,0.388,"mocked"],[9.787,0.138,"by"],[9.938,0.1,"the"],[10.05,0.562,"wise"],[10.988,0.537,"Inspire"],[11.537,0.15,"them"],[11.7,0.562,"instead"],[12.537,0.125,"by"],[12.675,0.3,"doing"],[12.988,0.175,"your"],[13.175,0.225,"own"],[13.412,0.312,"work"],[13.738,0.4,"well"],[14.15,0.113,"and"],[14.275,0.35,"without"],[14.637,0.787,"attachment"],[15.8,0.65,"Example"],[16.462,0.5,"teaches"],[16.975,0.225,"more"],[17.212,0.175,"than"],[17.4,0.713,"argument"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Dedicate All Your Actions to God (or Truth)","visual":["Do every duty with a spiritual frame of mind","Free from desire, attachment and grief","Dedicate each action to the Divine"],"L":["L8"],"say":"Lesson eight. Dedicate all your actions to God, or to truth. Krishna asks Arjuna to fight with his mind fixed on the Divine, free from desire, attachment and grief. That inner dedication changes the meaning of every act, even the hardest one.","start":351.6,"at":352.176,"end":369.96,"words":[[0.125,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.6,0.475,"eight"],[1.438,0.675,"Dedicate"],[2.125,0.188,"all"],[2.325,0.175,"your"],[2.513,0.512,"actions"],[3.038,0.113,"to"],[3.163,0.388,"God"],[3.775,0.1,"or"],[3.888,0.15,"to"],[4.05,0.537,"truth"],[4.95,0.525,"Krishna"],[5.487,0.412,"asks"],[5.912,0.55,"Arjuna"],[6.475,0.113,"to"],[6.6,0.325,"fight"],[6.938,0.113,"with"],[7.062,0.15,"his"],[7.225,0.388,"mind"],[7.625,0.338,"fixed"],[7.975,0.1,"on"],[8.088,0.087,"the"],[8.188,0.512,"Divine"],[9.025,0.237,"free"],[9.275,0.188,"from"],[9.475,0.588,"desire"],[10.238,0.65,"attachment"],[10.988,0.1,"and"],[11.1,0.512,"grief"],[12.012,0.237,"That"],[12.262,0.275,"inner"],[12.55,0.775,"dedication"],[13.338,0.487,"changes"],[13.838,0.1,"the"],[13.95,0.375,"meaning"],[14.338,0.1,"of"],[14.45,0.3,"every"],[14.762,0.388,"act"],[15.438,0.2,"even"],[15.65,0.075,"the"],[15.738,0.487,"hardest"],[16.238,0.312,"one"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Everyone Acts According to Their Own Nature","visual":["Even the wise act according to their nature","Forcing an unnatural path brings strain","Your own dharma, done imperfectly, is better"],"L":["L9"],"say":"Lesson nine. Everyone acts according to their own nature. Even the wisest person follows their deep nature, their svabhava. Forcing yourself into a path that is completely unnatural to you brings strain and failure. Krishna says it is better to do your own duty imperfectly than another's perfectly.","start":369.96,"at":370.536,"end":390.96,"words":[[0.125,0.438,"Lesson"],[0.575,0.487,"nine"],[1.438,0.512,"Everyone"],[1.962,0.35,"acts"],[2.325,0.512,"according"],[2.85,0.113,"to"],[2.975,0.138,"their"],[3.125,0.263,"own"],[3.4,0.562,"nature"],[4.338,0.3,"Even"],[4.65,0.087,"the"],[4.75,0.537,"wisest"],[5.3,0.512,"person"],[5.825,0.425,"follows"],[6.263,0.138,"their"],[6.412,0.312,"deep"],[6.737,0.5,"nature"],[7.463,0.138,"their"],[7.612,0.775,"svabhava"],[8.775,0.45,"Forcing"],[9.238,0.487,"yourself"],[9.738,0.263,"into"],[10.012,0.075,"a"],[10.1,0.438,"path"],[10.55,0.138,"that"],[10.7,0.1,"is"],[10.812,0.537,"completely"],[11.363,0.637,"unnatural"],[12.012,0.125,"to"],[12.15,0.225,"you"],[12.387,0.312,"brings"],[12.713,0.475,"strain"],[13.2,0.175,"and"],[13.387,0.562,"failure"],[14.325,0.463,"Krishna"],[14.8,0.35,"says"],[15.162,0.138,"it"],[15.312,0.138,"is"],[15.463,0.3,"better"],[15.775,0.113,"to"],[15.9,0.138,"do"],[16.05,0.2,"your"],[16.262,0.212,"own"],[16.488,0.5,"duty"],[17.0,0.838,"imperfectly"],[17.85,0.15,"than"],[18.012,0.45,"another's"],[18.475,0.713,"perfectly"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Likes and Dislikes Are the Two Great Stumbling Blocks","visual":["Likes and dislikes live in the senses","Do not come under their control","They are the two great stumbling blocks"],"L":["L10"],"say":"Lesson ten. Likes and dislikes are the two great stumbling blocks. Attraction and aversion are natural to the senses. The danger is letting them decide for you. Notice them, but do not hand them the wheel.","start":390.96,"at":391.536,"end":406.776,"words":[[0.138,0.45,"Lesson"],[0.6,0.487,"ten"],[1.462,0.438,"Likes"],[1.913,0.1,"and"],[2.025,0.675,"dislikes"],[2.712,0.138,"are"],[2.862,0.125,"the"],[3.0,0.25,"two"],[3.263,0.3,"great"],[3.575,0.475,"stumbling"],[4.062,0.55,"blocks"],[4.987,0.725,"Attraction"],[5.725,0.163,"and"],[5.9,0.65,"aversion"],[6.562,0.1,"are"],[6.675,0.575,"natural"],[7.263,0.1,"to"],[7.375,0.1,"the"],[7.487,0.7,"senses"],[8.588,0.113,"The"],[8.713,0.562,"danger"],[9.287,0.175,"is"],[9.475,0.338,"letting"],[9.825,0.15,"them"],[9.988,0.487,"decide"],[10.488,0.188,"for"],[10.688,0.35,"you"],[11.4,0.5,"Notice"],[11.912,0.275,"them"],[12.45,0.175,"but"],[12.637,0.113,"do"],[12.762,0.2,"not"],[12.975,0.275,"hand"],[13.262,0.163,"them"],[13.438,0.087,"the"],[13.537,0.463,"wheel"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Lust (Intense Desire) Is the Root Enemy of Wisdom","visual":["Lust is intense desire for pleasure","Unfulfilled, it becomes anger","It clouds wisdom like smoke covers fire"],"L":["L11"],"say":"Lesson eleven. Lust, intense desire, is the root enemy of wisdom. When desire is frustrated, it turns into anger, and when it persists, it clouds judgment the way smoke covers a fire or dust covers a mirror. Krishna calls it the enemy within.","start":406.776,"at":407.352,"end":425.16,"words":[[0.138,0.487,"Lesson"],[0.637,0.613,"eleven"],[1.637,0.525,"Lust"],[2.362,0.463,"intense"],[2.837,0.6,"desire"],[3.7,0.138,"is"],[3.85,0.113,"the"],[3.975,0.312,"root"],[4.3,0.3,"enemy"],[4.612,0.113,"of"],[4.737,0.537,"wisdom"],[5.675,0.188,"When"],[5.875,0.463,"desire"],[6.35,0.138,"is"],[6.5,0.713,"frustrated"],[7.4,0.125,"it"],[7.537,0.312,"turns"],[7.862,0.25,"into"],[8.125,0.463,"anger"],[8.812,0.138,"and"],[8.963,0.15,"when"],[9.125,0.113,"it"],[9.25,0.625,"persists"],[10.125,0.113,"it"],[10.25,0.412,"clouds"],[10.675,0.463,"judgment"],[11.15,0.075,"the"],[11.238,0.188,"way"],[11.438,0.4,"smoke"],[11.85,0.275,"covers"],[12.137,0.062,"a"],[12.213,0.475,"fire"],[12.7,0.113,"or"],[12.825,0.4,"dust"],[13.238,0.3,"covers"],[13.55,0.05,"a"],[13.613,0.4,"mirror"],[14.375,0.55,"Krishna"],[14.938,0.338,"calls"],[15.287,0.163,"it"],[15.463,0.15,"the"],[15.625,0.375,"enemy"],[16.012,0.55,"within"]]},{"layout":"steps","headline":"The ladder within","visual":["Body","Senses","Mind","Intellect","Spirit"],"L":["L12"],"say":"Lesson twelve. The path to overcoming lust is to master the ladder of the self. The senses are higher than the body. The mind is higher than the senses. The intellect is higher than the mind. And the Spirit is higher still. Know the Spirit, steady the mind with the intellect, and you can defeat this mighty enemy.","start":425.16,"at":425.736,"end":447.432,"words":[[0.138,0.438,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.625,"twelve"],[1.613,0.125,"The"],[1.75,0.362,"path"],[2.125,0.138,"to"],[2.275,0.588,"overcoming"],[2.875,0.475,"lust"],[3.362,0.15,"is"],[3.525,0.125,"to"],[3.663,0.45,"master"],[4.125,0.1,"the"],[4.237,0.35,"ladder"],[4.6,0.1,"of"],[4.713,0.1,"the"],[4.825,0.55,"self"],[5.775,0.113,"The"],[5.9,0.613,"senses"],[6.525,0.125,"are"],[6.662,0.412,"higher"],[7.088,0.163,"than"],[7.263,0.1,"the"],[7.375,0.425,"body"],[8.2,0.113,"The"],[8.325,0.412,"mind"],[8.75,0.15,"is"],[8.912,0.362,"higher"],[9.287,0.163,"than"],[9.463,0.087,"the"],[9.562,0.725,"senses"],[10.688,0.113,"The"],[10.812,0.625,"intellect"],[11.45,0.125,"is"],[11.588,0.375,"higher"],[11.975,0.163,"than"],[12.15,0.087,"the"],[12.25,0.55,"mind"],[13.2,0.125,"And"],[13.338,0.1,"the"],[13.45,0.525,"Spirit"],[13.988,0.125,"is"],[14.125,0.35,"higher"],[14.488,0.525,"still"],[15.4,0.25,"Know"],[15.662,0.113,"the"],[15.787,0.512,"Spirit"],[16.562,0.35,"steady"],[16.925,0.087,"the"],[17.025,0.388,"mind"],[17.425,0.138,"with"],[17.575,0.087,"the"],[17.675,0.625,"intellect"],[18.587,0.087,"and"],[18.688,0.113,"you"],[18.812,0.15,"can"],[18.975,0.463,"defeat"],[19.45,0.188,"this"],[19.65,0.388,"mighty"],[20.05,0.4,"enemy"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Two Paths Exist — Self-Knowledge and Selfless Action","visual":["Self-knowledge, for the contemplative","Selfless action, for everyone else","Both lead to the same goal"],"L":["L13"],"say":"Lesson thirteen. Two paths exist: self-knowledge and selfless action. The spiritual path is not one size fits all. The contemplative may walk the path of knowledge. Most of us, living active lives, walk the path of selfless work. Both arrive at the same place.","start":447.432,"at":448.008,"end":468.12,"words":[[0.125,0.487,"Lesson"],[0.625,0.775,"thirteen"],[1.762,0.25,"Two"],[2.025,0.425,"paths"],[2.462,0.55,"exist"],[3.337,0.8,"self-knowledge"],[4.15,0.163,"and"],[4.325,0.5,"selfless"],[4.838,0.525,"action"],[5.763,0.113,"The"],[5.888,0.588,"spiritual"],[6.487,0.463,"path"],[6.963,0.163,"is"],[7.138,0.263,"not"],[7.412,0.263,"one"],[7.688,0.375,"size"],[8.075,0.275,"fits"],[8.363,0.35,"all"],[9.113,0.1,"The"],[9.225,0.875,"contemplative"],[10.113,0.225,"may"],[10.35,0.35,"walk"],[10.713,0.1,"the"],[10.825,0.3,"path"],[11.137,0.1,"of"],[11.25,0.562,"knowledge"],[12.2,0.362,"Most"],[12.575,0.113,"of"],[12.7,0.338,"us"],[13.25,0.338,"living"],[13.6,0.388,"active"],[14.0,0.525,"lives"],[14.787,0.287,"walk"],[15.088,0.1,"the"],[15.2,0.325,"path"],[15.537,0.1,"of"],[15.65,0.475,"selfless"],[16.137,0.475,"work"],[16.988,0.275,"Both"],[17.275,0.463,"arrive"],[17.75,0.113,"at"],[17.875,0.1,"the"],[17.988,0.287,"same"],[18.288,0.588,"place"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Hypocrisy Is Worse Than Honest Action","visual":["Holding the body still while the mind indulges","Krishna calls this hypocrisy","Real discipline is inner"],"L":["L14"],"say":"Lesson fourteen. Hypocrisy is worse than honest action. Someone who outwardly renounces pleasures but inwardly dwells on them is deceiving themselves. Better to act honestly in the world with a disciplined mind than to pretend to renounce it.","start":468.12,"at":468.696,"end":485.232,"words":[[0.125,0.438,"Lesson"],[0.575,0.725,"fourteen"],[1.7,0.8,"Hypocrisy"],[2.513,0.2,"is"],[2.725,0.388